<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Vincent (island)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint Vincent is a volcanic island of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/windward-islands">Windward Islands</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. It long remained in the hands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinago">Kalinago</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garifuna">Garifuna</a>, people of mixed African and Kalinago descent, who resisted European settlement. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> gained it in 1763, deported most Garifuna after the war of 1795–1797, and it is now part of Saint Vincent and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grenadines">Grenadines</a>.</p></div>
